  "body": "## What changed\n\nA Circular ring was a closed polygon of 512 chords at every radius, and the helix entry's fallback ramp (\"the helix stands down to a ramp along the first cut\") walked that polygon back and forth. One Ø6 hole was 74,131 moves of 0.006 mm.\n\n- **Ring cut = two half-turn arcs** about the authored centre at each level (`crates/motion/src/machining2d/circular.rs`, `ring_walk`). G3 for climb, G2 otherwise, starting at the same +X point the polygon started at, so travel direction and climb are unchanged. The ladder walks them through `run_level_walks`, the same `Seg::Arc` walk Bore and Contour use.\n- **Polygon sized by tolerance, not 512.** The ring polygon is still used for planning: descent placement, links and the length of the zig-zag ramp. Its chord count is now the fewest power of two from 8 to 512 whose sagitta is within `ARC_FIT_TOL` (0.01 mm), for example 32 for R1. A power of two divides the 512-gon that the cutter-centre disk certificate is built from, so every ring vertex is still a certificate vertex and descents certify exactly as before.\n- **The ring ramp flies helical arcs** (`links::push_zig_ring`). It keeps the same out-and-back legs and the same travelled length, so the ramp angle is unchanged. Each leg is at most two half turns, the same pieces `entry::helix_about` already posts. Only Circular opts in (`Motion::with_ring_zig`). Pocket, Bore, Contour and every other ladder keep `push_zig` byte for byte.\n- Entry choice, lead, ramp angle, stepdown, stepover, ring-major sequencing and the verify laws are all unchanged.\n\n## Move counts: the issue's table, before and after\n\nFixture: a 40 x 40 x 10 plate with a modeled Ø6 through hole, `EM-0400-2FL`, the issue's MCP params (seeded Circular plus its patch), whole-model source. The **before** column is upstream main 7bfb1824 on the same fixture and reproduces the issue's numbers exactly.\n\n| Circular params | before | after | arcs after | warnings before -> after |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| repro (helix R1, stepover 0.5) | 74,131 | **417** | 364 | 0 -> 0 |\n| `entry: plunge` | 13,416 | **156** | 52 | 0 -> 0 |\n| `helix_radius: 0.5` | 13,446 | **186** | 108 | 28 -> 28 (the same XY-crossing warnings the issue reports) |\n| `stepover: 1.0` | 26,937 | **159** | 132 | 0 -> 0 |\n| `stepover: 2.0` | 26,937 | **159** | 132 | 0 -> 0 |\n| `radius: 4.0` | 26,858 | **338** | 208 | gouges -> gouges (12,585 -> 345, fewer moves to flag), post still held |\n| `radius: 6.0` | 53,690 | **650** | 416 | gouges -> gouges (37,544 -> 811), post still held |\n| `stepdown: 2.0` | 67,989 | **345** | 316 | 0 -> 0 |\n\nThe radius 4 and 6 rows cut past the modeled Ø6 wall, so they are gouges both before and after. The arcs are judged, not waved through.\n\n## Pins (each mutation-checked)\n\n- `crates/app/tests/circular_arcs.rs::the_issue_table_posts_arcs_and_verifies_the_same`: every row above has a move ceiling (repro <= 500), at least two arcs per ring-level, the same gouge verdict (in-hole rows clean, radius 4 and 6 still gouges).\n- `crates/motion/tests/circular_arcs.rs`:\n  - `the_issue_hole_posts_a_few_hundred_moves_not_tens_of_thousands`: the repro is under 500 moves with plunge, helix and ramp entries.\n  - `each_ring_level_is_two_half_turn_arcs_about_the_centre`: exactly 52 arcs (2 rings x 13 levels x 2). Each has centre = authored centre, endpoints on R1 or R0.5, a diametric half turn, is planar, has `ccw == climb` (both senses tested), and the first one starts at the polygon's old start.\n  - `the_ramp_rides_the_ring_as_helical_arcs`: every ramp move is a falling helical arc about the centre on the ring, out and back legs pair up, at most 12 per ring-level.\n- `circular.rs` unit test `ring_chords_are_sized_by_the_tolerance`: the sagitta is within `ARC_FIT_TOL`, the count is the fewest power of two that does it, it divides 512, R1 gives 32, and NaN falls back to 512.\n\nMutations, each red, then restored and green:\n- Old `circular.rs` (512 chords, no arcs): all 3 motion pins red. The app pin is red with \"74131 moves over 500\".\n- `with_ring_zig()` dropped (ramp back to chords): the ramp pin and the move-count pin are red.\n- First half arc's `ccw` flipped: the direction pin is red.\n- `ring_chords` forced to 512: the tolerance unit test is red.\n- `ring_chords` compared against 20 x tol: the tolerance unit test is red.\n\n## Gates\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green. Motion: lib plus center_cut_law, chamfer_circular, circular_arcs, control_comp, corner_blend, entry_approach, level_links, predrilled_entry, refusal_ghost, tiny_step, wear_comp, xy_arc_entry. App: bore_entry, circular_arcs, control_comp, ladder_entry_height, wear_comp.\n- Also green:\n  - app: circular_entity_law, circular_pick, circular_pick_law, operations, verify, posting, golden_cl, solid_law_goldens, recorded_post_streams, mill2d_b, units_in_refusals, arc_entry\n  - motion: machining2d, entry_arc\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Goldens\n\n**None changed.** No CL or NC golden, recorded post stream or solid-law golden is generated from a Circular op (golden_cl, solid_law_goldens and recorded_post_streams are green with no edits). No snapshot PNGs were touched.\n\n## Breaking?\n\nNo. This is a `fix:` that changes the posted output of existing Circular operations: the same circles, depths, direction and entries, in far fewer blocks. Nothing is removed. No parameter, command, project-file field or MCP shape changes. The reasoning is in `docs/decisions/1558-circular-arcs.md`.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No real post into a controller or the Hub sim. The arcs are the same `Move::arc` shape the helix entry already posts, and `posting` is green.\n- No release-lane heavy suites and no Windows run.\n- The vault mode uses the same ring walk. It is covered by `chamfer_circular` and `mill2d_b` (green), with no new vault-specific pin.\n- Posts without helical-arc support: the helix entry already emits helical arcs on every post, and this adds no capability gate.\n\nChangelog: Circular posts each ring as two arcs (G2/G3) and its ramp entry as helical arcs on the ring, instead of 512 fixed chords per ring: a Ø6 hole drops from 74,131 moves to 417 (#1558)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFork synced at upstream main 7bfb1824.\n\nFixes #1558\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
